  "body": "## The gap\n\n`tests/api/test_docs_bundle_wheel.py` builds a real wheel behind `MCC_WHEEL_TESTS=1` — gated deliberately after the nested-`uv` hang (5.49-era) — but nothing ever sets that flag: grep across `.github/`, `scripts/`, `Makefile` finds zero setters, and `git log -S MCC_WHEEL_TESTS` confirms it was never wired. The end-to-end half of the docs-bundle guarantee was decorative: every source-checkout check could stay green while the shipped wheel's Docs bundle broke.\n\n## The fix\n\nNew `wheel-e2e.yml`: **manual dispatch + weekly schedule (Wed 02:41 UTC)** — deliberately never on `push`/`pull_request`, so it cannot gate merges. Runs the real wheel build + bundle assertions on `windows-latest` under `MCC_WHEEL_TESTS=1`. Least privilege (`contents: read`), concurrency-grouped, 30-minute timeout sized against the fixture's own 900s build cap. Action SHAs copied from `tests.yml`.\n\nBeyond the brief: a new contract test (`tests/contracts/test_wheel_e2e_workflow.py`, 140 lines) enforces the properties that keep this honest over time — flag set nowhere except this workflow, action pins identical to tests.yml, no push/pull_request triggers, YAML parses.\n\nAlso documents the flag and schedule in `docs/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md`.\n\n## Verification\n\nLane ran ruff/ty/targeted pytest green locally; Windows CI itself validated statically only (YAML parse, trigger audit, pin comparison vs tests.yml) since the whole point is a runner environment — first real run is via manual dispatch after merge.\n\nNon-production change (.github/docs/tests only) — no version bump.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe scheduled run costs ~10–30 CI-minutes weekly on windows-latest. First execution happens post-merge via dispatch; if the cold-cache build exceeds 30 min the timeout needs one raise.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
