    "message": "fix(ci): arm the wheel e2e guard that could never run\n\nBroken: the five built-wheel assertions in tests/api/test_docs_bundle_wheel.py\nskipped on every CI run because their fixture gates on MCC_WHEEL_TESTS=1 and\nnothing anywhere set that flag (.github/, scripts/, Makefile: zero hits), so\nthe end-to-end wheel guarantee was decorative.\n\nMechanism: the gate exists deliberately -- a nested `uv build` inside\n`uv run pytest` contended for the project lock and hung CI until the fixture\nwas gated in the 5.49 era -- so the flag must not be set on the merge path.\n\nFix: new dispatch/schedule-only workflow .github/workflows/wheel-e2e.yml\n(never push/pull_request, cannot gate merges): windows-latest, Wednesdays\n02:41 UTC cron \"41 2 * * 3\" (off-minute/off-hour), contents:read permissions,\nconcurrency group with cancel-in-progress, timeout-minutes 30 (> the\nfixture's own 900s build cap), actions checkout/setup-uv SHA-pinned\nidentically to tests.yml, `uv sync` then `uv run --no-sync pytest` with\nMCC_WHEEL_TESTS=1 targeting only tests/api/test_docs_bundle_wheel.py\n(--no-sync keeps the outer uv off the lock while the fixture builds).\n\nDocs: section 6 in docs/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md records what runs, when, and\nwhat a red run means.\n\nVerification: yaml.safe_load parse + trigger exactness confirmed; new\ntests/contracts/test_wheel_e2e_workflow.py pins all nine properties (9\npassed); ruff format/ruff check clean; uv run ty check clean; mutation\nchecks broke every guard (env drop, pull_request trigger, SHA flip, cron\n:30, timeout 10, sync rename, contents:write, cancel-in-progress false,\nworkflow rename) -- each caught by its named test, bytes restored identical.\nWindows CI itself not executable locally: validated statically per lane.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
